IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `rta-road`
IMPORT `rta-qa`

-- Road Traffic Act 1974 (WA) -- cases for the Q&A layer (rta-qa.l4): every exported question, for every role and
-- every situation.
--
-- Each question is asked for the roles it is not about, with every other input an ASSUMEd value that has none: the
-- answer must be `does not arise for you`, and reading a BOOLEAN or NUMBER input that is ASSUMEd stops the evaluation
-- with an error. Each question with a situation input is asked, for each role it is about, with the situation FALSE
-- and every later input ASSUMEd. Those two groups are generated from the parameter lists (scratchpad qa_params.py),
-- and come last. The hand-worked cases come first: each answer is worked by hand from the deposited text, and for the
-- baseline's seat (the rider and the driver) each question is also asserted equal to the baseline export's answer on
-- the same facts. Life facts: Jake (au/wa cradle-to-grave-jake), k042 and k083, as in rta-cases-road.l4; every other
-- fixture is HYPOTHETICAL.
--
-- Two enumerations the baseline reads through OTHERWISE (`Where I am riding` in r 210B and r 15, `Why I am not
-- authorised` in s 49) do not fail when an ASSUMEd value is read (graffiti finding 31). They are read only after the
-- role and the situation, which the parameter script checks are read first, so their "not read" cases rest on that
-- order as well as on the evaluation.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases -- the Q&A layer`

ASSUME `an unasked fact` IS A BOOLEAN
ASSUME `an unasked number` IS A NUMBER
ASSUME `an unasked Where I am riding` IS A `Where I am riding`
ASSUME `an unasked Why I am not authorised` IS A `Why I am not authorised`
ASSUME `an unasked Why the driver was not authorised` IS A `Why the driver was not authorised`

`as the rider` MEANS `I ride an electric scooter, skateboard or similar device`
`as the driver` MEANS `I drive a car, motorcycle or other motor vehicle`
`as the employer` MEANS `I employ someone to drive, or let someone drive my vehicle`

`Jake's e-scooter, as a record` MEANS `My device` WITH
    `it has at least 1 wheel` IS TRUE
    `it is designed for a single person` IS TRUE
    `it has an electric motor` IS TRUE
    `it has an effective stopping system` IS TRUE
    `top speed on its motor alone on level ground, in km/h` IS 25
    `length in mm` IS 1100
    `width in mm` IS 600
    `height in mm` IS 1200
    `unladen mass in kg` IS 18
    `it meets other mass and dimension requirements the Minister has approved` IS FALSE
    `it has pedals` IS FALSE
    `it is a motorised scooter, motorised wheelchair, electric personal transporter or wheeled toy` IS FALSE

`Jake on the 60 km/h road, as a record` MEANS `My ride` WITH
    `where I am` IS `a carriageway`
    `the speed limit of the carriageway, in km/h` IS 60
    `I am only crossing the carriageway, by the shortest safe route` IS FALSE
    `I am only avoiding an obstruction, for no longer than necessary` IS FALSE
    `I pass a no wheeled devices sign` IS FALSE
    `a no bicycles sign or marking applies here` IS FALSE
    `my speed, in km/h` IS 20

`Jake on the footpath at 15 km/h, as a record` MEANS `My ride` WITH
    `where I am` IS `a footpath`
    `the speed limit of the carriageway, in km/h` IS 60
    `I am only crossing the carriageway, by the shortest safe route` IS FALSE
    `I am only avoiding an obstruction, for no longer than necessary` IS FALSE
    `I pass a no wheeled devices sign` IS FALSE
    `a no bicycles sign or marking applies here` IS FALSE
    `my speed, in km/h` IS 15

`Jake's 80 km/h zone, as a record` MEANS `Where I am driving` WITH
    `a sign sets the limit here (speed zone, school zone in its hours, shared zone or speed limited area)` IS TRUE
    `the signed limit, in km/h` IS 80
    `I am in a built-up area` IS FALSE
    `I am towing, over 12 t GVM, or driving a bus over 5 t GVM` IS FALSE

`Jake 25 km/h over, as a record` MEANS `My driving` WITH
    `I was driving without the owner's consent` IS FALSE
    `I have never held a licence or permit` IS FALSE
    `I am a person described in s 49(3)(a), (b), (ca), (c) or (da)` IS FALSE
    `my licence does not cover this kind of vehicle` IS FALSE
    `I am committing an offence under the ATD Act s 38(1)` IS FALSE
    `km/h above the speed limit` IS 25
    `I was driving to escape pursuit by a police officer` IS FALSE

`a disqualified driver's second drive, as a record` MEANS `My unlicensed drive` WITH
    `I was riding an electric rideable device` IS FALSE
    `I am authorised under the ATD Act Part 2 to drive this vehicle` IS FALSE
    `I drove under the ATD Act s 11(1) regulations or a s 49A necessity permit` IS FALSE
    `why I am not authorised` IS `I was refused, disqualified, cancelled or suspended, or am in a prescribed class (s 49(3)(a), (b), (ca), (c), (da))`
    `this is a subsequent offence under s 49(6)` IS TRUE

`0.085 on a first offence, as a record` MEANS `My drinking and driving` WITH
    `my blood alcohol content, in g per 100 mL` IS 0.085
    `I am a novice driver (ATD Act s 40(2))` IS FALSE
    `I am otherwise a person s 64A(2) lists (drink-driving disqualification, extraordinary licence, recently disqualified)` IS FALSE
    `my vehicle is one s 64A(5) lists (bus with passengers, hire passengers, GCM 22.5 t or more, dangerous goods)` IS FALSE

`the never licensed reason` MEANS `I never held a licence of the kind needed, or it expired or I surrendered it`
`the novice reason` MEANS `I am a type 1A novice driving between midnight and 5 a.m. or over the passenger limit`
`the penalty enforcement reason` MEANS `I lost my licence under penalty enforcement laws (s 49(3)(d))`
`the disqualified reason` MEANS `I was refused, disqualified, cancelled or suspended, or am in a prescribed class (s 49(3)(a), (b), (ca), (c), (da))`
`their never licensed reason` MEANS `they never held a licence of the kind needed, or it had expired or been surrendered`
`their novice reason` MEANS `they were a type 1A novice driving between midnight and 5 a.m. or over the passenger limit`
`their penalty enforcement reason` MEANS `they had lost their licence under penalty enforcement laws (s 49(3)(d))`
`their disqualified reason` MEANS `they were refused, disqualified, cancelled or suspended, or in a prescribed class (s 49(3)(a), (b), (ca), (c), (da))`

