§§ `For the person who employs someone to drive, or lets someone drive their vehicle`

-- s 49(1)(b): letting an unlicensed person drive is an offence; not if I did not employ or permit them (then nothing
-- else is read), they rode an eRideable (r 55(2)(h)), were authorised all the same, or it was driven under the s 11(1)
-- regulations or a necessity permit (s 49(2)).
